+## Running children
+
+`list_active()` returns an immutable `ActiveSubagent` snapshot of every delegated child running in
+this process, whether `delegate_task` or `launch` started it. It needs no handle and no active turn,
+so a plugin route or background thread can call it.
+
+```python
+for child in ctx.subagent_lifecycle.list_active():
+    print(child.subagent_id, child.session_id, child.parent_session_id, child.status)
+```
+
+Each snapshot has `subagent_id`, `session_id` (the child's own session, which follows a compaction),
+`parent_subagent_id` (`None` for a child of a top-level session), `parent_session_id` (the session
+that owns the delegation), `depth`, `goal`, `model`, `status`, `started_at`, and `steerable`
+(`False` once the child stopped accepting steering, just before it finishes). A finished child
+leaves the list.
+
+`steer_active(subagent_id, text)` queues text for a listed child by its id, the same in-process
+steering `delegate_task` uses. It does not check who owns the child: the plugin decides who may
+steer it. It returns `False` for empty text, an unknown or finished child, or a child that is not
+`steerable`.
+
